1
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,970
Miyata-kun.

2
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:15,800
Yeah?

3
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:19,570
What are you reading?

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,810
Oh, this?

5
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,180
Sh...

6
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:32,490
Sh... A book for people going to Shuisu.

7
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:34,910
Shuisu?

8
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:37,820
It's Switzerland.

9
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:38,900
Switzerland.

10
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:44,180
Climbing the Alps, eating
cheese fondue, that sort of thing.

11
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,090
It sounds amazing.

12
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:49,840
I'd love to go too.

13
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:58,300
Why so serious while
reading such a fun travel book?

14
00:00:58,470 --> 00:00:59,470
Ah...

15
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:01,850
Oh...

16
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:08,810
"Editing Techniques to
Survive the Publishing Winter."

17
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:13,320
That's a pretty unique
title for a travelogue.

18
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:20,660
Hey.

19
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,050
We finally made it out here.

20
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:26,620
Let's just forget about work.

21
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,460
At least while we're on vacation.

22
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:36,690
I want you to think only of me.

23
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,760
Only of Senpai?

24
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:43,910
Yeah, only of me.

25
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,040
Please don't ask the impossible.

26
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,110
I see.

27
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:57,610
Looks like even Iwanaga
Takashi is powerless here.

28
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:06,000
What's that?

29
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:07,360
Hmm?

30
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:11,210
It tracks my physical activity
and quantifies the data.

31
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,000
Pretty cool, right?

32
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,420
You bought something
expensive again, didn't you?

33
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:24,720
A good earner never
worries about going broke.

34
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,030
Miyata-kun, come on in.

35
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:46,910
I'm good.

36
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,806
You're always harping on about
getting your money's worth.

37
00:02:49,830 --> 00:02:52,270
And you're going to leave
without swimming even once?

38
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:54,670
Is it that time already?

39
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:20,150
Wow, it's freezing!

40
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:23,580
Hold on!

41
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:27,080
Stop splashing!

42
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:28,449
Miyata-kun, that's too much!

43
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:30,540
Didn't you start it?

44
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,380
So cold!

45
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:29,600
"Love is Better the Second Time Around season2"
(Episode 1)

46
00:04:51,910 --> 00:04:54,870
I went for the vibe.

47
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:57,679
So I definitely got my money's worth.

48
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:00,020
My, how mature and composed of you.

49
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:02,630
I am 32, after all.

50
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,939
Didn't we just celebrate
your birthday recently?

51
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,140
I remember.

52
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,720
Good.

53
00:05:10,010 --> 00:05:12,520
I wish you'd relax a bit more.

54
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:14,640
I can't.

55
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:19,309
Someone like you, with a wealthy
background and a secure job...

56
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:20,730
...probably wouldn't understand.

57
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:25,399
Just trying to survive this endless
crisis in the publishing industry...

58
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,300
...takes everything I
have every single day.

59
00:05:30,490 --> 00:05:31,490
Ah.

60
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:34,870
It's Pentas.

61
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:36,920
Pentas?

62
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:41,020
Look, it has five petals, right?

63
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:45,300
Its name comes from the Greek word
"Pente," meaning "five."

64
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:48,340
When do you even memorize this stuff?

65
00:05:49,050 --> 00:05:51,360
Hmm, I just picked it up along the way.

66
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:54,420
That's kind of annoying.

67
00:05:57,810 --> 00:05:59,660
What about this one?

68
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:01,120
Petunia.

69
00:06:01,610 --> 00:06:03,930
Its etymology comes from an
indigenous Brazilian language.

70
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:06,170
It means tobacco.

71
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:12,180
Iwanaga Takashi.

72
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,330
The man who used to be
a dark chapter in my past.

73
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,270
Miyata-kun.

74
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:23,210
Why don't we just run away together?

75
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:35,770
The man who once toyed with me...

76
00:06:37,770 --> 00:06:38,810
...betrayed me...

77
00:06:39,850 --> 00:06:41,360
...and abandoned me.

78
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:44,170
Nice to meet you.

79
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:46,960
I'm Miyata Akihiro from Tokyo Commercial.

80
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,450
Nice to meet you.

81
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,720
I don't think this is
our first time meeting.

82
00:06:54,030 --> 00:06:55,079
Miyata-kun.

83
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:58,330
Meeting that kind of man again...

84
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:03,750
Honestly, I truly felt his looks
were his only redeeming quality.

85
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:06,270
Just that face.

86
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,550
I'm pretty amazing, right?

87
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:13,029
So hurry up and praise me.

88
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:14,820
You're doing great, Miyata-kun.

89
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:17,060
Say it with a little more feeling.

90
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:27,080
I'm Miyata, the one who
promised to elope with Takashi-san.

91
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:29,360
I want to be with you, Miyata-kun.

92
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:31,950
I'll follow you.

93
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:37,210
Forever.

94
00:07:38,110 --> 00:07:39,110
For the rest of my life.

95
00:07:40,810 --> 00:07:42,000
No matter where.

96
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:46,190
I fell in love all over again.

97
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:49,360
It's not like I went out
of my way to learn it.

98
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:52,730
Miyata-kun?

99
00:07:56,750 --> 00:07:58,030
Don't tell me...

100
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:00,020
...you're mesmerized by me?

101
00:08:02,370 --> 00:08:04,150
Please don't flatter yourself.

102
00:08:13,350 --> 00:08:15,740
- I'm home.
- I'm home.

103
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,160
- That was fun.
- Yeah, it was.

104
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:27,250
Ah, I'll put this in the fridge.

105
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,480
Thanks.

106
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:37,180
I'd love to have your
curry again, Miyata-kun.

107
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:39,470
- You got it.
- Really?

108
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:40,640
- No problem.
- Thanks.

109
00:08:42,150 --> 00:08:44,520
I'll put this in too...

110
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:59,300
Getting tired of vacuuming?

111
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:02,720
Please don't treat me like an idiot.

112
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:04,770
This fell on the floor.

113
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:05,950
Ah...

114
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,600
Thanks.

115
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:09,860
That's a nice watch.

116
00:10:10,230 --> 00:10:11,570
Where did you get it?

117
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:14,030
Someone gave it to me
back when I was a student.

118
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:18,200
You probably can't even
buy this model anymore.

119
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,360
I see.

120
00:10:21,990 --> 00:10:24,070
Let's find a different style
for our couple watches.

121
00:10:25,470 --> 00:10:26,470
Okay...

122
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,870
It's already been two years
since we moved in together.

123
00:10:43,890 --> 00:10:46,370
We've grown much closer than before.

124
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,150
But even so...

125
00:10:55,650 --> 00:10:56,740
Cheers.

126
00:10:57,690 --> 00:11:01,070
I still feel like there's so
much I don't know about him.

127
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,660
Don't drink so fast.

128
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:05,990
I know.

129
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,580
You get drunk so easily.

130
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:24,690
So...

131
00:11:25,990 --> 00:11:29,310
Who gave you that watch?

132
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:33,160
Someone I was very close to in college.

133
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:37,400
Does that mean...

134
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:42,070
Did you two date?

135
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:46,160
Yeah.

136
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:48,580
We dated.

137
00:11:50,426 --> 00:11:53,466
Seriously, you should
have told me sooner.

138
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:55,290
It's not that big of a deal.

139
00:11:56,210 --> 00:11:58,550
It is a big deal.

140
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:02,430
Please don't hide things
from me. Just tell me straight.

141
00:12:03,510 --> 00:12:06,310
I don't really want to talk about my ex.

142
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,270
I've told you that before, haven't I?

143
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:10,230
Yeah...

144
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,390
You did say that...

145
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:15,440
You're the only one I
want to be with right now.

146
00:12:18,690 --> 00:12:20,360
Isn't that enough?

147
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:44,360
See, didn't I warn you?

148
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:47,930
Don't be mad.

149
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:53,330
Don't go saying you can't make the
meeting tomorrow because of a hangover.

150
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:58,570
Don't worry.

151
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:03,290
Senpai.

152
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:04,820
Hmm?

153
00:13:07,230 --> 00:13:08,660
Come here.

154
00:13:33,650 --> 00:13:38,650
You get incredibly sexy
when you're drunk.

155
00:13:41,450 --> 00:13:43,570
You love that about me, don't you?

156
00:13:50,110 --> 00:13:51,110
Yeah.

157
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:55,960
I love you the most.

158
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:00,840
Is that all?

159
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:04,400
Not just that.

160
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:07,990
I love you.

161
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:26,700
You've gotten really good
at this too, Miyata-kun.

162
00:14:29,010 --> 00:14:31,880
I'm still nowhere near your level, Senpai.

163
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:36,160
You think so?

164
00:15:06,310 --> 00:15:09,340
But to me, Senpai,
you're my first...

165
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,930
...and only man.

166
00:15:15,590 --> 00:15:18,330
I really hope it stays this way forever.

167
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:25,770
Then what am I to you, Senpai?

168
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:32,320
I feel the same way.

169
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:25,860
Good morning.

170
00:16:27,630 --> 00:16:29,320
Good morning.

171
00:17:14,910 --> 00:17:16,570
Here you go.

172
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:18,370
Huh?

173
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:20,450
This works wonders for a hangover.

174
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:24,580
Thanks.

175
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:27,380
You're welcome.

176
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:36,929
With prices continuing to rise, food-related
issues are also drawing a lot of attention.

177
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,889
Ah, it's Professor Hibino.

178
00:17:38,890 --> 00:17:42,700
From a current economic perspective,
what do you think is the most important?

179
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:44,730
Well...

180
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:46,399
While there are many challenges...

181
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:50,150
...I believe agricultural
policy is a crucial topic.

182
00:17:50,770 --> 00:17:53,250
He's as eloquent as ever.

183
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:58,580
Actually, we've been thinking about
asking him to write for our magazine.

184
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:01,200
I see...

185
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,390
Is something wrong?

186
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:08,930
Just remembering some things from the past.

187
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,130
Hibino-san was my upperclassman in college.

188
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:15,250
Oh, is that so?

189
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:19,600
No wonder you're interested
in Hibino-san, Miyata-kun.

190
00:18:20,330 --> 00:18:21,330
That guy...

191
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:24,100
...has always been incredibly popular.

192
00:18:25,890 --> 00:18:27,890
I don't want to ask him
just because he's handsome.

193
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,190
True.

194
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:33,146
You've always been a stickler for
keeping things professional, Miyata.

195
00:18:33,170 --> 00:18:34,650
Because didn't you say that before?

196
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:38,780
"If I work with Teacher Iwanaga,
I won't be able to control my feelings."

197
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:41,249
"So I want to step down as his editor."

198
00:18:41,250 --> 00:18:42,869
The way you phrased
that is highly problematic.

199
00:18:42,870 --> 00:18:44,490
But it's the truth, isn't it?

200
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:49,470
It's much better than those who
work with me with ulterior motives.

201
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,250
That sounds really harsh.

202
00:18:57,150 --> 00:19:00,890
This won't just boost Japan's
food self-sufficiency rate...

203
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:02,769
What time are you coming home today?

204
00:19:02,770 --> 00:19:04,640
Probably around six.

205
00:19:04,690 --> 00:19:06,169
- What about you, Miyata-kun?
- Same here.

206
00:19:06,170 --> 00:19:07,429
Let's have dinner together then.

207
00:19:07,430 --> 00:19:08,490
Sounds good.

208
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:11,210
Oh.

209
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:15,320
This is that apartment building
they're constructing near our place, right?

210
00:19:15,690 --> 00:19:18,610
Wow, so this is what
it's going to look like.

211
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:19,910
It's really beautiful.

212
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:22,620
It's bigger than our current place.

213
00:19:23,310 --> 00:19:25,150
Maybe it wouldn't be a
bad idea to move there.

214
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,590
I can't afford that.

215
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:35,070
Huh?

216
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:37,550
I don't have that kind of money.

217
00:19:38,090 --> 00:19:40,730
Splitting our current rent
is already pushing my limits.

218
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,329
Good morning.

219
00:19:49,330 --> 00:19:50,410
Good morning.

220
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:51,850
Morning.

221
00:19:51,851 --> 00:19:52,890
Good morning.

222
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:55,250
Good morning.

223
00:19:55,690 --> 00:19:56,690
Oh, morning.

224
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:58,440
Ah, Miyata-kun.

225
00:19:58,550 --> 00:20:01,780
How's the project with
Teacher Iwanaga coming along?

226
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:02,950
It's going really well.

227
00:20:03,290 --> 00:20:05,119
I'm scheduled to have a
meeting with him today.

228
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,540
Ah, I see.

229
00:20:10,290 --> 00:20:13,380
By the way, have you seen this?

230
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,690
Teacher Iwanaga's interview.

231
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:20,009
He mentioned he has
someone special in his life.

232
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,590
Yes, I've seen it.

233
00:20:22,010 --> 00:20:23,970
Man, that was a real surprise.

234
00:20:24,010 --> 00:20:26,730
To think Teacher Iwanaga would
actually talk about his private life.

235
00:20:27,010 --> 00:20:30,520
He must have had a major change of heart.

236
00:20:30,890 --> 00:20:32,520
Who knows?

237
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,650
So...

238
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:42,380
Miyata-kun, could you add some juicy topics
like this to your project?

239
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:44,160
Huh?

240
00:20:44,490 --> 00:20:46,990
This kind of gossip
about Teacher Iwanaga...

241
00:20:48,510 --> 00:20:50,640
I'm sure there are readers
who'd love to see it.

242
00:20:51,710 --> 00:20:53,420
Chief, what's gotten into you?

243
00:20:54,130 --> 00:20:57,540
Didn't you use to hate
this kind of gossip?

244
00:21:00,010 --> 00:21:01,050
Miyata-kun.

245
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:05,390
Haven't you heard that "Bessatsu Tosho"
is being discontinued?

246
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:07,280
What?

247
00:21:08,670 --> 00:21:11,680
"Business Now" could follow
in its footsteps at any moment.

248
00:21:12,890 --> 00:21:15,060
If we don't publish a bestseller soon...

249
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:17,480
Our department is doomed.

250
00:21:20,090 --> 00:21:21,320
Excuse me.

251
00:21:26,930 --> 00:21:28,080
Shiraishi-kun.

252
00:21:28,410 --> 00:21:29,620
What's wrong?

253
00:21:31,350 --> 00:21:33,330
You have a visitor.

254
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:35,080
Hmm?

255
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:36,950
Is it Miyata-kun?

256
00:21:38,390 --> 00:21:39,390
No.

257
00:21:40,390 --> 00:21:42,830
I shouldn't have any other
appointments scheduled.

258
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,429
Miyata-kun will be here any minute.

259
00:21:45,430 --> 00:21:47,950
Could you tell the guest to wait a moment?

260
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:53,780
If it's Miyata-san, you guys could
just have the meeting at home, right?

261
00:21:54,330 --> 00:21:55,640
Come on.

262
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:58,110
Just let him wait outside.

263
00:22:00,510 --> 00:22:03,780
You really don't want to
give us your blessing, do you?

264
00:22:05,820 --> 00:22:08,220
Well, that's not included in my salary.

265
00:22:08,570 --> 00:22:12,300
Besides, the guest who's here today...

266
00:22:13,450 --> 00:22:15,870
I don't think it's a good
idea to keep him waiting.

267
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:20,630
Professor, please come in.

268
00:22:40,790 --> 00:22:42,940
It's been a while, Iwanaga-kun.

269
00:22:46,150 --> 00:22:47,590
Hibino-san...

270
00:22:48,490 --> 00:22:50,510
Thank you, Shiraishi-kun.

271
00:22:54,370 --> 00:22:56,010
I bet this sudden visit startled you.

272
00:22:57,790 --> 00:22:59,420
What on earth are you doing here?

273
00:23:00,310 --> 00:23:03,130
I happened to have an
appointment nearby this morning.

274
00:23:03,410 --> 00:23:06,400
I was planning to head
straight back to Osaka right after.

275
00:23:06,670 --> 00:23:09,760
But I felt like I just had
to drop by and see you.

276
00:23:11,910 --> 00:23:15,930
It's all because I read this
on the bullet train here.

277
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:28,000
I've been dying to see you.

278
00:23:46,010 --> 00:23:47,389
(Next Episode Preview)
Hold me tight.

279
00:23:47,390 --> 00:23:49,010
I'm not good enough for you.

280
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:52,390
His taste has certainly changed a lot.

281
00:23:52,690 --> 00:23:54,430
I hope you won't be so jealous.

282
00:23:54,470 --> 00:23:57,640
Please don't lose to him Professor Hibino.

283
00:23:58,090 --> 00:23:59,270
Let's start over.
